    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes and the test is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic and keyed the household on `(lastName, postcode)`, per the specification.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n   - `householdId(Owner)` now computes `HH-` + first 12 upper-hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`. It's a pure function of `(lastName, postcode)`, so owners sharing both derive the same id regardless of creation order \u2014 and it's now assigned to every owner, not just when a match pre-exists.\n   - `applyHousehold(owner, sharesHousehold)` sets the computed `householdId` and, if any existing owner derives the same one, treats it as a **household duplicate**: rejected with 409 unless the request sets `sharesHousehold=true`, in which case the owner is created as a declared member. `sharesHousehold` no longer *creates* the link (the link is derived) \u2014 it only *bypasses the duplicate block*. The old address-based matching + back-fill logic is gone.\n   - `flagPossibleDuplicate(owner, sharesHousehold)` now short-circuits to `possibleDuplicate=false` for a declared member \u2014 a declared household member is not a suspected duplicate.\n   - Duplicate detection continues to key off `householdId` (via `identityKey`), which now flows from the computed value.\n\n2. **`HouseholdDuplicateException.java`** (new) + handler in **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2192 returns **409 Conflict** with `errors: [\"household\"]`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `sharesHousehold` and `householdId` descriptions to reflect keying on `(lastName, postcode)` and the \"bypass-only\" semantics.\n\n**On the membership level:** the spec text mentioned \"the household-size input to the membership level,\" but this codebase's `membershipLevel` formula (base 1, +1 for email, +1 for no namesakes) has no household-size input and nothing else references household size, so there was nothing to re-point at the computed id.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId` passes (same lastName+postcode share the id; the second owner is accepted only via `sharesHousehold`; a different lastName yields a different id), and `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
